/*
 * TestArm64SemanticsSimd.cpp
 *
 * Tests of the A64 lifter of the scalar floating point, Advanced SIMD and
 * cryptographic instructions (Arm64SemanticLiftSimd.cpp...): the rows of
 * tests/arm/Arm64SimdSemanticRows*.inc, generated by tests/arm/tools/
 * gen_simd_semantic_rows*.py from an independent Python model of the Arm ARM
 * pseudocode (not by running dismount), run by the interpreter: the start
 * state, an instruction, the state it must leave.
 *
 * The differential tests against Unicorn and the M4 (tests/arm/semantics)
 * cover what those processors implement; these rows pin the exact values of
 * the edge cases (NaN propagation, the exception flags, the saturation flag,
 * the rounding modes) and cover the instructions neither processor runs (the
 * FP8 family, FAMINMAX, FPRCVT, LUT).
 *
 * Author: Elad Raz <e@eladraz.com>
 */
